        "path": "packages/tempod/src/config.ts",
        "line": 6,
        "text": "The fix changes `process.env[\"TEMPO_BUILD_ID\"]` to `process.env.TEMPO_BUILD_ID`, claiming `bun build --env` inlines the dot-property but not the bracket-property. This is load-bearing for deploy correctness: if `TEMPO_BUILD_ID` is not inlined, every image still reports `pkg.version` and the new verification in `scripts/deploy-worker.ts` fails only if the running binary already happens to contain a matching string, so the `CLONE_FAILED` image-staleness bug could persist. I could not corroborate the minifier/inlining behavior from docs/build config in this repo, so this should be confirmed before merge.",
        "blocking": false,
        "evidence": {
          "quote": "export const VERSION: string = process.env.TEMPO_BUILD_ID || pkg.version;",
          "why": "The deploy verification below checks that `/usr/local/bin/tempod` contains `buildId`, which relies on this compile-time inlining. Without repository proof that bun behaves as described in IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md, the fix may not actually set VERSION to the deploy's build id at build time."
        }
      }
